    "bio": "A Representative from Texas; born in Bonham, Fannin County, Tex., February 23, 1951; B.A., Bethany Nazarene College (now Southern Nazarene University), Bethany, Okla., 1974; attended Nazarene Theological Seminary, Kansas City, Mo., 1975-1976; real estate developer; member of the Carrollton, Tex., city council, 1980-1984; mayor of Carrollton, Tex., 1984-1987; member of the Texas state house of representatives, 1987-2004; elected as a Republican to the One Hundred Ninth and to the seven succeeding Congresses (January 3, 2005-January 3, 2021); was not a candidate for reelection to the One Hundred Seventeenth Congress in 2020.",
